#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro2.md:6
msgid "The `proc_macro2` Crate"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro2.md:8
msgid ""
"The built-in `proc_macro` crate is tightly coupled to the compiler "
"internals, meaning its types cannot be instantiated or manipulated outside "
"of the compiler's plugin environment."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro2.md:12
msgid ""
"The **`proc_macro2`** library is a standard third-party crate that mirrors "
"the entire API of the built-in `proc_macro` crate, with some key advantages:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro2.md:15
msgid ""
"**Unit testing:** You can write standard unit tests for your procedural "
"macros because `proc_macro2::TokenStream` can be instantiated and asserted "
"on in standard library tests."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro2.md:18
msgid ""
"**Standalone execution:** It allows libraries to work with token streams in "
"other execution contexts, such as build scripts (`build.rs`) or binary CLI "
"tools."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro2.md:21
msgid ""
"**Seamless interoperability:** Types from `proc_macro2` are easily converted "
"to and from standard `proc_macro` types using `.into()`."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro2.md:26
msgid ""
"Mention that `proc_macro2` is an essential dependency for almost any "
"procedural macro crate."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro2.md:28
msgid ""
"This is because testing is incredibly important for macro development, and "
"`proc_macro2` makes it possible to write unit tests that parse strings into "
"token streams and assert on the outputs."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/proc_macro2.md:31
msgid ""
"Popular libraries like `syn` and `quote` fully rely on `proc_macro2` types "
"as their base inputs/outputs."
msgstr ""
